  "description": "An empty USRSEC on a first entry: STARTBR's WHEN DFHRESP(NOTFND) arm at :600-606. Nothing was received, so USRIDINI still holds the LOW-VALUES :117 moved into COUSR0AO - COUSR0AO REDEFINES COUSR0AI at COUSR00.CPY:373, so one MOVE sets both views - and :218 therefore takes its first leg and :219 anchors the browse on LOW-VALUES. GTEQ is commented out at :592, so the STARTBR positions on an equal key rather than on the first key at or after the anchor; either way a dataset holding no record cannot satisfy it and CICS answers NOTFND. The arm opens with a bare CONTINUE at :601, and the statements after it DO execute - USER-SEC-EOF is set at :602, 'You are at the top of the page...' is moved to WS-MESSAGE at :603-604, the cursor is planted at :605 and the map is sent at :606 - which is the single easiest thing to get wrong here. It raises no error flag, so :286 still admits the rest of PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD: :288 is false for ENTER so no record is discarded, :292's guard fails so INITIALIZE-USER-DATA at :446 never runs and the ten rows keep the LOW-VALUES that :117 left them at rather than the spaces :450 onwards would have written, the loop at :300 never iterates, and in the ELSE at :317-322 WS-IDX is still 1 so the short-page increment at :320-321 is NOT taken and the page number stays 00000000. That zero is the assertion: an empty file leaves the operator on page zero, not page one. :327 and :328 DO run, because the error flag is off, so PAGENUMO carries 00000000 and USRIDINO carries spaces - which is precisely what separates this case from case19, where the same paragraph is entered with the flag on and both fields keep their LOW-VALUES. The ordered EVALUATE at :597 lands on its second arm and never on WHEN OTHER (gate G30); with case17 and case19 this case completes the STARTBR / READNEXT / READPREV outcome matrix (gate G47); the dataset is declared empty at its copybook width, so the 80-byte record contract is asserted without inventing a row (gates G19 and G21); and RETURN-CODE stays 0 because an online program does not abend here. Every expected value is statically derived by structured reading of app/cbl/COUSR00C.cbl, cross-checked against app/cpy-bms/COUSR00.CPY for the 59 field widths, app/cpy/CSUSR01Y.cpy for the 57-into-80 record layout and app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy for the commarea; none of it was captured from a run of the legacy program, which is empirically impossible in this environment (AAP risk R-A).",
